content="<think>\nAlright, I need to fix the Ansible playbook so that it passes ansible-lint. Let me look at the errors reported.\n\nFirst, the errors mention using FQCN for certain modules. I see that the modules 'group', 'user', 'copy', and 'meta' are being used without their full package names. Ansible now prefers using the FQCN, which includes the namespace like 'ansible.builtin'.\n\nSo, I'll update each module call to use the FQCN. For example, 'group' becomes 'ansible.builtin.group'.\n\nNext, there's an issue with the octal value '0600'. Ansible-lint doesn't like implicit octal values. I should convert it to decimal. 0600 in octal is 384 in decimal, so I'll change it to 384.\n\nI also need to ensure that the playbook structure remains correct. The tasks should be in the same order, and only the necessary changes are made without altering functionality.\n\nLet me go through each task:\n\n1. For creating the etcd group, replace 'group' with 'ansible.builtin.group'.\n2. For creating the etcd user, replace 'user' with 'ansible.builtin.user'.\n3. For copying the file, change 'copy' to 'ansible.builtin.copy' and update the mode to 384.\n4. For flushing handlers, replace 'meta' with 'ansible.builtin.meta'.\n\nI'll make these changes and ensure the YAML syntax is correct. That should fix all the linting issues.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Create etcd group\n  ansible.builtin.group:\n    name: etcd\n    state: present\n\n- name: Create etcd user\n  ansible.builtin.user:\n    name: etcd\n    group: etcd\n    shell: /bin/nologin\n    comment: Etcd user\n    state: present\n\n- name: Copy systemctl config file for kernel hardening\n  ansible.builtin.copy:\n    src: rke2-cis-sysctl.conf\n    dest: /etc/sysctl.d/60-rke2-cis.conf\n    mode: 384\n    remote_src: true\n  notify: Restart systemd-sysctl\n\n- name: Flush handlers\n  ansible.builtin.meta:\n    flush_handlers: true\n```" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-