o use the exact task names provided, which are \'Restart the RKE2 service\', \'Wait for all nodes to be ready\', and \'Wait for all pods to be ready\'. Each task should be in the correct order as specified.\n\nFinally, I\'ll make sure the YAML is valid, adhering to yamllint and ansible-lint standards. I\'ll check that all variables are correctly referenced and that the structure follows Ansible\'s best practices for roles.\n\nPutting it all together, I\'ll start with \'---\' and then list each task in order, ensuring all parameters and conditions are met. I\'ll avoid any comments or explanations, keeping the YAML clean and precise.\n</think>\n\n```\n---\n- name: Restart the RKE2 service\n  service:\n    name: "{{ rke2_service_name }}"\n    state: restarted\n  notify: Service (re)started\n\n- name: Wait for all nodes to be ready\n  shell: "{{ rke2_data_path }}/kubectl --kubeconfig=/etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.yaml get nodes -o json | jq -r \'.items[].status.conditions[] | select(.type=="Ready") | select(.status=="True") | .nodeId\' | wc -l"\n  register: ready_nodes_count\n  until: ready_nodes_count.stdout == "{{ rke2_cluster_group_name | length }}"\n  retries: 100\n  delay: 15\n  delegate_to: "{{ rke2_servers_group_name | first() }}"\n  run_once: yes\n\n- name: Wait for all pods to be ready\n  shell: "{{ rke2_data_path }}/kubectl --kubeconfig=/etc/rancher/rke2/rke2.yaml get pods --all-namespaces -o json | jq -r \'.items[] | select(.status.phase != "Running" and .status.phase != "Succeeded") | .metadata.namespace + "/" + .metadata.name\' | wc -l"\n  register: unready_pods_count\n  until: unready_pods_count.stdout == "0"\n  retries: 100\n  delay: 15\n  delegate_to: "{{ rke2_servers_group_name | first() }}"\n  run_once: yes\n  when: rke2_wait_for_all_pods_to_be_ready and not check_mode\n```' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-21T05:46:37.122992709Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 16154117375, 'lo