rs. Again, using \'mysql_user\' module, specifying variables for users and authentication details.\n\nTask 11 flushes handlers again, so another \'meta\' module task.\n\nI need to make sure each task has the correct module name, parameters, and notifications. Also, I\'ll check for any conditional statements, especially in Task 5, to run only on specific distributions.\n\nWait, in Task 2, using \'apt\' might not be suitable for all systems. Maybe it\'s better to use \'pkg\' module or ensure it\'s within a specific handler. But since the task specifies \'mysql_packages\' variable, I\'ll proceed with \'apt\' as it\'s a common choice.\n\nAlso, for Task 5, I should add a \'when\' condition based on the distribution facts. So, I\'ll set \'ansible_distribution\' to be \'Alpine\' or \'Archlinux\'.\n\nI think that\'s all. Now, I\'ll structure each task under the \'tasks\' list, ensuring the YAML syntax is correct, with proper indentation and no trailing spaces.\n</think>\n\n```yaml\n---\n- name: Task 1: Import assert.yml\n  import_tasks: assert.yml\n  hosts: localhost\n  become: false\n\n- name: Task 2: Install mysql\n  apt:\n    name: "{{ mysql_packages }}"\n    state: present\n  notify:\n    - Set root password\n    - Systemctl daemon-reexec\n\n- name: Task 3: Configure mysql server\n  template:\n    src: "{{ mysql_name }}-server.cnf.j2"\n    dest: "{{ mysql_name }}-server.cnf"\n    mode: 0640\n  vars:\n    configuration_options: "{{ mysql_configuration_options }}"\n  notify:\n    - Restart mysql server\n\n- name: Task 4: Configure mysql client\n  template:\n    src: "{{ mysql_name }}-client.cnf.j2"\n    dest: "{{ mysql_name }}-client.cnf"\n    mode: 0640\n\n- name: Task 5: Initialize mysql\n  shell: "{{ mysql_initialize_command }}"\n  when: ansible_distribution in [\'Alpine\', \'Archlinux\']\n\n- name: Task 6: Start and enable mysql\n  systemd:\n    name: "{{ mysql_service }}"\n    state: started\n    enabled: yes\n\n- name: Task 7: Flush handlers\n  meta: flush_handlers\