ould resolve the linting errors.\n\nLet me write out the corrected playbook with the FQCNs. I\'ll replace \'apt\' with \'ansible.builtin.apt\' and \'apt_repository\' with \'ansible.builtin.apt_repository\'.\n\nI think that\'s all. The tasks should now pass ansible-lint because the modules are correctly specified with their FQCNs.\n</think>\n\n---\n- name: Install Ansible package\n  ansible.builtin.apt:\n    name: ansible\n    state: "{{ ansible_package_state }}"\n\n- name: Enable EPEL repository\n  ansible.builtin.apt_repository:\n    repo: "{{ ansible_epel_repo_name }}"\n    state: present' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'deepseek-r1:14b', 'created_at': '2025-10-21T06:02:36.987235351Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 9213198678, 'load_duration': 109087116, 'prompt_eval_count': 1197, 'prompt_eval_duration': 513425245, 'eval_count': 585, 'eval_duration': 8589114574, 'model_name': 'deepseek-r1:14b'} id='run--7a085553-8c19-498c-9689-e21ed267cf2d-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 1197, 'output_tokens': 585, 'total_tokens': 1782}
